WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.900
HIPAA training. Module 8. Enforcement, penalties and real-world cases.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.133
OCR investigates complaints and breach reports.

3
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:15.567
Most cases end before a penalty, and good faith helps.

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.233
A complaint or breach report reaches OCR.

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:24.100
OCR decides whether HIPAA applies.

6
00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:28.067
It asks for policies, risk analyses and records.

7
00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:32.367
Guidance, an agreement with a plan, or a penalty.

8
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.233
Civil penalties rise with what the organization knew.

9
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:40.967
Willful neglect, not fixed, is the top tier.

10
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:44.800
Then willful neglect, fixed within 30 days.

11
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.867
Then reasonable cause.

12
00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:49.200
And not knowing at the bottom.

13
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.833
Knowingly disclosing health information: up to 1 year.

14
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.833
Under false pretenses: up to 5 years.

15
00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:01.267
For gain or malicious harm: up to 10 years.

16
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.433
Opening records with no work reason.

17
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.567
A stolen laptop and no risk analysis to show.

18
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.933
A patient story posted without a signed authorization.

19
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.667
Stop.

20
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.067
Do not share.

21
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.600
Ask your lead.

22
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.733
Now read the module.
